    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To solve the given expression \\(\\frac{235^2 - 221^2}{14}\\), we can use the difference of squares formula, which states \\(a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\\). Here, \\(a = 235\\) and \\(b = 221\\). Let's break down the steps:\n\n1. Use the difference of squares formula:\n   \\[\n   235^2 - 221^2 = (235 - 221)(235 + 221)\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate the values:\n   \\[\n   235 - 221 = 14\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   235 + 221 = 456\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   235^2 - 221^2 = 14 \\times 456\n   \\]\n\n3. Substitute this result into the original expression:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{235^2 - 221^2}{14} = \\frac{14 \\times 456}{14}\n   \\]\n\n4. Simplify the expression by canceling the common factor:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{14 \\times 456}{14} = 456\n   \\]\n\nLet's verify this using Python code to ensure accuracy.\n```python\n# Define the values\r\na = 235\r\nb = 221\r\n\r\n# Calculate the difference of squares using the difference of squares formula\r\ndifference_of_squares = (a - b) * (a + b)\r\n\r\n# Calculate the final result\r\nresult = difference_of_squares / 14\r\nprint(result)\n```\n```output\n456.0\n```\nThe calculated value of \\(\\frac{235^2 - 221^2}{14}\\) is \\(\\boxed{456}\\).",
